{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 11, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "-1-i = sqrt(2)*e^(-i*3pi/4)\n  = sqrt(2)*(cos(-3pi/4) + i*sin(-3pi/4))\n  r = |z| = sqrt(2),  theta = arg z = -3pi/4\n  theta is the principal argument, -pi < theta <= pi\n  check: equal numerically (-1 - 1i, complex arithmetic)\n  check: equal numerically (-1 - 1i, complex arithmetic)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 11, "ok": true, "cmd": "polar", "ucas": "polar -1-i", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "polar", "input": "-1-i", "exponential": "sqrt(2)*e^(-i*3pi/4)", "trigonometric": "sqrt(2)*(cos(-3pi/4) + i*sin(-3pi/4))", "r": "sqrt(2)", "theta": "-3pi/4"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "value", "points": 1, "max_diff": 1.570092458683775e-16, "passed": true}, {"kind": "value", "points": 1, "max_diff": 1.570092458683775e-16, "passed": true}], "files": [], "text": "-1-i = sqrt(2)*e^(-i*3pi/4)\n  = sqrt(2)*(cos(-3pi/4) + i*sin(-3pi/4))\n  r = |z| = sqrt(2),  theta = arg z = -3pi/4\n  theta is the principal argument, -pi < theta <= pi\n  check: equal numerically (-1 - 1i, complex arithmetic)\n  check: equal numerically (-1 - 1i, complex arithmetic)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 12, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "the 3 cube roots of -1 (w^3 = -1)\n  w0 = 1/2 + i*sqrt(3)/2      = e^(i*pi/3)  (principal)\n  w1 = -1                     = e^(i*pi)\n  w2 = 1/2 - i*sqrt(3)/2      = e^(-i*pi/3)\n  check: each w^3, parsed back as printed, equals -1 numerically\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 12, "ok": true, "cmd": "nthroots", "ucas": "nthroots 3 -1", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "nthroots", "roots": [{"k": 0, "re": 0.5000000000000001, "im": 0.8660254037844386, "polar": "e^(i*pi/3)", "exact": "1/2 + i*sqrt(3)/2", "principal": true}, {"k": 1, "re": -1, "im": 0, "polar": "e^(i*pi)", "exact": "-1", "principal": false}, {"k": 2, "re": 0.5000000000000001, "im": -0.8660254037844386, "polar": "e^(-i*pi/3)", "exact": "1/2 - i*sqrt(3)/2", "principal": false}], "headline": "the 3 cube roots of -1 (w^3 = -1)"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "each w^3, parsed back as printed, equals -1 numerically"}], "files": [], "text": "the 3 cube roots of -1 (w^3 = -1)\n  w0 = 1/2 + i*sqrt(3)/2      = e^(i*pi/3)  (principal)\n  w1 = -1                     = e^(i*pi)\n  w2 = 1/2 - i*sqrt(3)/2      = e^(-i*pi/3)\n  check: each w^3, parsed back as printed, equals -1 numerically\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 13, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "the 4 fourth roots of 1 (w^4 = 1)\n  w0 = 1                      = 1  (principal)\n  w1 = i                      = e^(i*pi/2)\n  w2 = -1                     = e^(i*pi)\n  w3 = -i                     = e^(-i*pi/2)\n  check: each w^4, parsed back as printed, equals 1 numerically\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 13, "ok": true, "cmd": "unity", "ucas": "unity 4", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "unity", "roots": [{"k": 0, "re": 1, "im": 0, "polar": "1", "exact": "1", "principal": true}, {"k": 1, "re": 0, "im": 1, "polar": "e^(i*pi/2)", "exact": "i", "principal": false}, {"k": 2, "re": -1, "im": 0, "polar": "e^(i*pi)", "exact": "-1", "principal": false}, {"k": 3, "re": 0, "im": -1, "polar": "e^(-i*pi/2)", "exact": "-i", "principal": false}], "headline": "the 4 fourth roots of 1 (w^4 = 1)"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "each w^4, parsed back as printed, equals 1 numerically"}], "files": [], "text": "the 4 fourth roots of 1 (w^4 = 1)\n  w0 = 1                      = 1  (principal)\n  w1 = i                      = e^(i*pi/2)\n  w2 = -1                     = e^(i*pi)\n  w3 = -i                     = e^(-i*pi/2)\n  check: each w^4, parsed back as printed, equals 1 numerically\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 14, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)\n  holomorphic: the Cauchy-Riemann equations hold at 64 sample points of [-2, 2] x [-2, 2] (df/dx = df/(i dy))\n  holomorphic except at sqrt (the branch cuts of the principal values)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 14, "ok": true, "cmd": "holomorphic", "ucas": "holomorphic sqrt(z)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "holomorphic", "var": "z", "holomorphic": true, "entire": false, "except": "sqrt (the branch cuts of the principal values)"}, "notes": [{"kind": "assumed", "text": "z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "cauchy_riemann", "points": 64, "max_diff": 9.045418441299049e-11, "passed": true, "text": "df/dx = df/(i dy) at sample points of [-2, 2] x [-2, 2]"}], "files": [], "text": "  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)\n  holomorphic: the Cauchy-Riemann equations hold at 64 sample points of [-2, 2] x [-2, 2] (df/dx = df/(i dy))\n  holomorphic except at sqrt (the branch cuts of the principal values)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 15, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)\nconj(z) is not holomorphic\n  Cauchy-Riemann fails: at z = 1/2 + i/4, df/dx = 1 but df/(i dy) = -1\n  (it uses conj, which is not holomorphic)\n  Wirtinger derivatives there: df/dz = 0, df/dconj(z) = 1 (holomorphic means df/dconj(z) = 0)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 15, "ok": true, "cmd": "holomorphic", "ucas": "holomorphic conj(z)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "holomorphic", "var": "z", "holomorphic": false, "counterexample": {"at": "1/2 + i/4", "df_dx": "1", "df_idy": "-1"}, "non_holomorphic_parts": "conj"}, "notes": [{"kind": "assumed", "text": "z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)\nconj(z) is not holomorphic\n  Cauchy-Riemann fails: at z = 1/2 + i/4, df/dx = 1 but df/(i dy) = -1\n  (it uses conj, which is not holomorphic)\n  Wirtinger derivatives there: df/dz = 0, df/dconj(z) = 1 (holomorphic means df/dconj(z) = 0)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 16, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)\nresidue of 1/(z^2 + 1) at z = i:\n  = -i/2\n  a pole of order 1 (|f| grows like |z - a|^-1)\n  computed as (1/(2 pi i)) times the integral of 1/(z^2 + 1) on |z - a| = 0.01 and 0.005 (512 points each): they agree\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 16, "ok": true, "cmd": "residue", "ucas": "residue 1/(z^2+1) at i", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "residue", "var": "z", "at": "i", "found": true, "residue": "-i/2", "re": 0, "im": -0.5000000000000001, "singularity": "pole", "order": 1}, "notes": [{"kind": "assumed", "text": "z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "circle_integrals", "points": 1024, "passed": true, "text": "radius 0.01 and 0.005 agree"}], "files": [], "text": "  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)\nresidue of 1/(z^2 + 1) at z = i:\n  = -i/2\n  a pole of order 1 (|f| grows like |z - a|^-1)\n  computed as (1/(2 pi i)) times the integral of 1/(z^2 + 1) on |z - a| = 0.01 and 0.005 (512 points each): they agree\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 17, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  note: atanh(2) is on the branch cut; the value is that of (log(1 + z) - log(1 - z))/2\natanh(2) = log(3)/2 - i*pi/2\n  Re = log(3)/2,  Im = -pi/2\n  check: equal numerically (0.5493061443 - 1.570796327i, complex arithmetic)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 17, "ok": true, "cmd": "complex", "ucas": "complex atanh(2)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "complex", "input": "atanh(2)", "result": "log(3)/2 - i*pi/2", "re": "log(3)/2", "im": "-pi/2"}, "notes": [{"kind": "info", "text": "atanh(2) is on the branch cut; the value is that of (log(1 + z) - log(1 - z))/2"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "value", "points": 1, "max_diff": 0, "passed": true}], "files": [], "text": "  note: atanh(2) is on the branch cut; the value is that of (log(1 + z) - log(1 - z))/2\natanh(2) = log(3)/2 - i*pi/2\n  Re = log(3)/2,  Im = -pi/2\n  check: equal numerically (0.5493061443 - 1.570796327i, complex arithmetic)\n"}, "isError": false}}
